review:
After years, I still find myself reinstalling this game from time to time. It is simply fun. At the normal level, it is challenging without being overwhelming.

I started having crashes on Windows 10 but a tip about disabling "Decals" in the configuration solved my issues.

Depending on my mood I can decide for:
- following the missions;
- take over a village, a city neighborhood, a military base;
- collect hidden stuff;
- car, boat, aircraft racing;
- wander around randomly blowing stuff.

I never tried the multiplayer stuff, single player has enough material for a lifetime.

Great open world third person action adventure with a huge open world and over the top action. Overall game is very fun and cathartic, but if you want to explore and do everything that game can offer it can get very repetitive. Easily can recommend for everyone who likes to cause chaos and distraction.

Pros:
- Enormous open world;
- Good optimisation;
- Great visuals;
- Grappling hook and parachute is very fun to use;
- Good vehicles controls;
- Tons things to do;

Cons:
- Repetitive location design;
- Technical problems;
- Poor enemy variety;
